@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Account and Worker Contact API
	Testing Koroneiki Account API functionality in relation to Worker Contacts.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Engr Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Automotive      |
	| Koroneiki Engineering     |

Scenario: Assign worker contact to account
	Koroneiki worker contacts should be able to be assigned to accounts.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                                  |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki     |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                             |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                     |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                             |
	| Region       | United States                            |
	| Status       | Approved                                 |
	| Tier         | Regular                                  |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              |
	And I assign worker contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be assigned the team "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Assign worker contact to account with special characters
	Koroneiki worker contacts should be able to be assigned to accounts with special characters in the description.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                                       |
	| Description           | 100% $$$$$ making & awesome org for our @customers! ^_^ v +-= |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                                                  |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                                          |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                                                  |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken                      |
	| Region                | United States                                                 |
	| Status                | Approved                                                      |
	| Tier                  | Regular                                                       |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com                                   | 
	And I assign worker contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be assigned the team "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Assign nonexistent worker contact to account
	Koroneiki worker contacts should be able to be created and assigned to accounts if the contact does not exist.

	Given I create a nested field for a nonexistent worker contact with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                 | KORAUTO                              |
	| Contact Nested Field | ${staticContactsNestedField}         |
	| Description          | Test automotive account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number           | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                 | Koroneiki Automotive                 |
	| Phone Number         | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Region               | United States                        |
	| Status               | Approved                             |
	| Tier                 | Regular                              |
	| Website              | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be assigned the team "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Assign nonexistent verified worker contact to account
	Koroneiki verified worker contacts should be able to be created and assigned to accounts if the contact does not exist.

	Given I create a nested field for a nonexistent worker contact with the following values
	| Email Address          | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                     |
	| First Name             | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language               | English                                  |
	| Last Name              | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name            | User                                     |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                 | KORAUTO                              |
	| Contact Nested Field | ${staticContactsNestedField}         |
	| Description          | Test automotive account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number           | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                 | Koroneiki Automotive                 |
	| Phone Number         | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Region               | United States                        |
	| Status               | Approved                             |
	| Tier                 | Regular                              |
	| Website              | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address          | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                     |
	| First Name             | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language               | English                                  |
	| Last Name              | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name            | User                                     |
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be assigned the team "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Assign worker contact and nonexistent worker contact to account
	Koroneiki worker contacts and non existent worker contacts should be able to be created and assigned to accounts.

	Given I create a nested field for a nonexistent worker contact with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I rename the first contact nested field variable
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact2                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a nested field for the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I rename the second contact nested field variable
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                 | KORAUTO                                                     |
	| Contact Nested Field | ${staticContactsNestedField1},${staticContactsNestedField2} |
	| Description          | Test automotive account on koroneiki                        |
